### Appendix E: Glossary

| Term | Meaning |
|---|---|
| Table turn time | How long a party occupies a table, including the time to prepare it for the next party |
| Guest wait time | How long guests wait to be seated or to be served |
| Average check | The average total amount billed per party |
| Comp | A meal that is not charged, for example when a remade order replaces one the guest sent back |
| POS (point of sale) | Software that manages prices, tracks orders, and generates the check |
| Host software | Software that tracks table usage and wait lists |
| FOH (front of house) | Servers, hosts, and other guest-facing staff |
| BOH (back of house) | Kitchen staff, bussers, runners, and other behind-the-scenes staff |
| Product mix | The balance of menu items guests order, which add-ons and promotions aim to improve |
| OKR | Objectives and Key Results, the company's goal-setting framework |
| Pilot | A small-scale trial used to test an idea before a wider rollout |
| Contribution margin | The share of revenue left after direct variable costs such as food and hourly labor |
| Misalignment | A situation where stakeholders do not agree on the details of the project |

